# SwiftFormat — SundayScaries. Run as `swiftformat --lint .` in CI; format locally with
# `swiftformat .`. Identical to ../FantasyKit/.swiftformat apart from the exclusions.
--swiftversion 6.0
--indent 4
--commas always
--trimwhitespace always
--maxwidth none
--wraparguments preserve
--wrapparameters preserve
--wrapcollections preserve
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--header ignore

# Options set to match conventions this codebase already follows (each one verified
# against a preview diff on 2026-09-05, not assumed):
#   --ifdef no-indent          code inside `#if DEBUG` is not indented
#   --ranges no-space          ranges are written `1...3`
#   --decimalgrouping ignore   `86_400` is the author's grouping; leave numbers alone
#   --semicolons inline        one-line test rows use `let a: A; let b: B`; only trailing ones go
--ifdef no-indent
--ranges no-space
--decimalgrouping ignore
--semicolons inline

# Disabled on purpose. SwiftFormat 0.63's defaults reflow statement bodies and rewrite
# code, which is a migration, not a lint. The rules below either fight a convention this
# codebase uses deliberately or change more than whitespace:
#   blankLinesAtStartOfScope   type and suite bodies open with a blank line here
#   consecutiveSpaces          aligned `case` tables and trailing comments are deliberate
#   wrap*Bodies                one-line `if x { return }` guards are idiomatic Swift
#   wrapMultilineStatementBraces, wrapIfExpressionBodies   same family
#   docComments                turns // into /// by heuristic; comment style is a review call
#   hoistTry, hoistAwait, conditionalAssignment, preferKeyPath   semantic-adjacent rewrites
#   opaqueGenericParameters, redundantPublic, redundantThrows, redundantAsync   change API shape
#   redundantSwiftUIGroup      view identity is load-bearing here (CLAUDE.md §6); no auto-unwrapping
#   sortImports                @testable imports are grouped after plain imports on purpose
#   noForceTryInTests, noForceUnwrapInTests   force unwrapping is allowed in tests (CLAUDE.md §1)
#   modifierOrder              SwiftLint owns modifier order (`nonisolated public`); the two
#                              defaults disagree and `--fix` passes would ping-pong six files
#   redundantLet               `let _ = x` inside a SwiftUI `body` is a statement; the bare `_ = x` it
#                              rewrites to is an expression the ViewBuilder rejects (broke WeeklyView)
--disable blankLinesAtStartOfScope,consecutiveSpaces,wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapPropertyBodies,wrapFunctionBodies,wrapLoopBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies,wrapMultilineStatementBraces,docComments,hoistTry,hoistAwait,conditionalAssignment,preferKeyPath,opaqueGenericParameters,redundantPublic,redundantThrows,redundantAsync,redundantSwiftUIGroup,sortImports,noForceTryInTests,noForceUnwrapInTests,modifierOrder,redundantLet
--exclude DerivedData,.build
